  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN vertices (numbered 111 through NNN).\n\nA simple path between two different vertices aaa and bbb (a&lt;ba \\lt ba&lt;b) is called a clamp path if it does not contain any vertices with numbers smaller then aaa or greater than bbb.\n\nCalculate the number of clamp paths in the given tree.",
    "constraints": [
      "2 ≤ N ≤ 2000",
      "The given graph is a tree."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains an integer N (2 ≤ N ≤ 2000) – the number of vertices of the tree. The second line contains N space‑separated integers p1 … pN. For each i (1 ≤ i ≤ N) if pi ≠ 0 there is an undirected edge between vertices i and pi. Exactly one pi equals 0 and denotes the root of the tree.",
    "outputFormat": "A single integer – the number of clamp paths in the given tree.",
